# Taste Skill — required for frontend changes

Whenever you create, edit, redesign, or style frontend/UI (components, pages, layouts, CSS, landing pages, marketing surfaces, visual polish):

1. **Read first** (before writing UI code):
   `.cursor/skills/design-taste-frontend/SKILL.md`
2. **Follow that skill fully** — brief inference, design direction, anti-slop rules, pre-flight check.
3. Do not ship generic AI UI (Inter/Roboto defaults, purple gradients, card soup, placeholder sections).

Skip this rule for pure backend, infra, docs-only, or non-UI tasks.

## Companion skills (use when the task matches)

| Situation | Skill path |
| --- | --- |
| Default / greenfield UI | `.cursor/skills/design-taste-frontend/SKILL.md` |
| Existing UI redesign / audit | `.cursor/skills/redesign-existing-projects/SKILL.md` |
| Soft / premium calm look | `.cursor/skills/high-end-visual-design/SKILL.md` |
| Minimalist / editorial | `.cursor/skills/minimalist-ui/SKILL.md` |
| Brutalist / industrial | `.cursor/skills/industrial-brutalist-ui/SKILL.md` |
| Image → code pipeline | `.cursor/skills/image-to-code/SKILL.md` |
| Incomplete / truncated output | `.cursor/skills/full-output-enforcement/SKILL.md` |

Default is always **design-taste-frontend**. Add a companion only when the request clearly needs it.
